  "notes": "\"The straight backbeat is the parameter that separates his records from the rest of this section\" — the entry says it in those words, so `halfTime` is false and the snare is `backbeat_24` with the section's driest programmed tone: \"a hard, dry programmed snare on **2&4 rather than half-time**, an 808 or sampled kick on 1 and the offbeat of 2, handclaps doubling the backbeat, minimal hat carpet, and live cymbal/tom overdubs\". The tempo spine is unusually specific for a producer entry — a straight 68–113 band \"with a marked **80–82 cluster** across his best-known placements\" — so `bpm.mode` is 81, which is one of the few producer modes in this section that is researched rather than inferred. ⛔ **`bass808` is null**: \"a fat analog synth bass or played electric bass with real syncopated motion, mixed loud and often distorted — not a sustained sliding 808.\" Harmony is \"4-bar and functional — Prince-lineage `i–VII–VI`, `I–IV–V` with blues sevenths — with real bridges and occasional modulation, i.e. genuinely progression-based rather than loop-based\", authored verbatim with the sevenths in `extensions`. \"His beds leave room for a guitar solo, which is rare in this lane\" is why the melody register is wide and the arrangement carries a real instrumental section. ⚠ He and the Miguel artist model are the same catalogue by design; the separation here is that this is the board — the drums and the low end carry the authored detail, and the melody block is plainer than the singer's. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the swing amount, every drum probability and the bassline figures; the entry says his gear and workflow \"are not documented on the reachable surface\". ⚠ `confidence` is medium, mirroring the entry. ⚠ **The last value in `session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry names four — \"B minor, A♭ major, C minor and A minor recur\" — and E♭ major is an authored addition that the research does not state.",
